  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you're stuck without internet. On our end your laptop shows as offline, so it isn't reaching the internet at all. Please try these steps in order and check after each one whether websites load:\n1. Turn Wi-Fi off and back on, or forget your home network and reconnect to it.\n2. Restart your laptop.\n3. Restart your home router: unplug it for 30 seconds, plug it back in, and wait a couple of minutes for it to come back up.\n4. If it still doesn't work, connect the laptop to your phone's hotspot (or plug in a network cable). That tells us whether the problem is the laptop or your home network.\n\nCan you also tell us whether other devices on your home Wi-Fi, like your phone or TV, can load websites? If none of them can, the problem is your home internet, and your internet provider would need to fix it.\n\nOnce you're back online, please keep the laptop on and signed in for about 30 minutes. It hasn't connected to our systems in about 12 days, so it needs time to catch up on updates. Reply with what you find, and let us know right away if none of this works.",
  "internal_note": "User 7 (Sofia Rossi, Marketing, working from home). Account is active, VPN access is true, not locked or blocked. Laptop BL-LT-0107 is offline, last check-in 2026-09-27, warning 'No check-in for 12 days' (KB-018 says follow up after 7 days). Gave the KB-014 home steps: Wi-Fi toggle or forget network, restart laptop, restart router, test on hotspot or wired. Asked whether other devices on her Wi-Fi work, to tell a home network fault from a laptop fault. Next steps: if her other devices also fail, it's her ISP and the ticket can be resolved. If only the laptop fails, including on a hotspot, escalate as a laptop network fault. Once she's online, run check_device_status again to confirm a fresh check-in (KB-018). If she's online but the device still doesn't check in after a restart, escalate per KB-018.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014",
    "KB-018"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
